 "title": "Recorder of Deeds | henry-county",
 "text": "-->\nRecorder of Deeds | henry-county\ntop of page\nHenry County, Missouri\nRecorder of Deeds\nGail A. Perrymann\n100 W Franklin\nClinton, Missouri 64735\nTelephone:(660)-885-7209\nE-mail: henrycountyrecorder@gmail.com\nOffice Hours: Monday thru Friday 8:30-4:30\n(Marriage licenses 8:30-4:00)\n​\nEmployees:\nAllison Millam, Deputy\nAbigayle Wagoner, Deputy\n​\nNeed a Certified Marriage License?\nAn agreement is necessary to begin the process of eRecording. To set up please contact:\niCounty Technologies, LLC\nPhone: 816.295.1540\nOr by e-mail to:\nDave Mudd - Email: Dave.mudd@icounty.com\nor\nLisa Norris - Email: Lisa.norris@icounty.com\nTo obtain a certified copy of a marriage license in order to get your Missouri Real ID, visit the courthouse where you applied for your license. Certified copies are $9.\nhttps://dor.mo.gov/driver-license/issuance/real-id/documents/RID.pdf\nReal Id documents\nThe Recorder of Deeds Office is the place where all transactions having to do with land are recorded and kept on file. Henry County land records start in the 1830’s.\nThe Recorder of Deeds Office does not create documents.\nWe record deeds that meet state requirements.\nThe Recorder of Deeds Office takes marriage license applications, issues marriage licenses, files the license after the marriage, and maintains a permanent record of the marriage.\nThe Recorder’s Office records surveys and plats of subdivisions.\nThe Recorder’s Office records Armed Forces discharge papers for all veterans who reside in the county. This is a free service.\nFederal and state tax liens are filed in the Recorder’s Office.\nAPPLICATION FOR MARRIAGE LICENSE\n​​​\nAs of August 28, 2025 the minimum age for marriage in Missouri is 18 years old.\nPLEASE NOTE: There is no option to get married at the Henry County Courthouse. If this is something you are interested in you will need to contact your Municipal Court or City Hall at 660-885-3485.\n​ As of August 28, 2007, there is no longer a waiting period for marriage licenses. Once a marriage license is picked up, it is good for thirty (30) days. The license can be used anywhere in the State of Missouri.\nREQUIREMENTS OF BRIDE AND GROOM\n​\nBoth bride and groom must be 18 years of age or older.\nBoth bride and groom must apply in person at the Recorder’s Office.\nBoth must bring proof of Social Security Number and date of birth. (Drivers license or Social security card and birth certificate are acceptable.)\nPayment of $55.00(no $100.00 bills) is due when license is picked up. Payment must be made in cash.\n​\n​\nFEE SCHEDULE FOR NON-CHARTER COUNTIES\nEFFECTIVE AUGUST 28,2026\nRECORDER ASSOCIATION OF MISSOURI\nDOCUMENT FORMATTING STANDARDS\nEFFECTIVE JANUARY 1, 2002\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\nREQUIREMENTS FOR STANDARD DOCUMENTS\n​\n​\nSIZE AND INK\nATTACHMENTS\nMARGINS\nFIRST PAGE DESIGNATIONS\nTitle of the document.\nDate of the document\nAll grantor’s names w/marital status\nAll grantee’s names\nAny statutory addresses\nLegal Description\nReference book and pages if required\nDESIGNATIONS:\nGrantors and grantees must be designated in order to be indexed. There is no limit as to Combinations or exclusions, but include the words ‘grantor‘ or ‘grantee‘. Note: It is the filer’s or preparer’s responsibility to make the designations.\nStatutory addresses must be designed , i.e. ‘Grantee’s Mailing Address’……\nThe address of the property shall not be accepted as a legal description.\nBook and page references required on certain documents, i.e. release deeds, assignments, etc must be designated.\nCOVER PAGES:\nEXEMPT DOCUMENT FROM THE FORMATTING REQUIREMENTS:\nFEES\nREJECTIONS:\n​\nAll documents that are rejected must be returned with a reason for rejection. The Recorder’s Association will develop a standard rejection form that can be used or adapted by any filing officer.\nHOME\nAssessor\nCounty Clerk\nCoroner\nCounty Commission\nPublic Administrator\nRecorder of Deeds\nSheriff’s Office\nSurveyor\nTreasurer/Collector\nSENIOR TAX RELIEF INFO\nDEPARTMENTS\nRoad and Bridge\nEmergency Management\nHenry County Emergency 911\nLEPC\nUniversity Extension\nCOURTS\nCircuit Court\nCircuit Clerk\nAssociate Court\nJuvenile Division\nProsecuting Attorney\nELECTIONS\nSample Ballot/Election Info\nAbsentee Voting\nPoll Workers\nRegistering to Vote\nHENRY COUNTY BUDGET/SALES TAX\nHenry County Budget\nSales-Tax\nPLANNING & ZONING\nInformation\nHELPFUL LINKS\nGenealogy Information\nState and Federal Links\nCommunity Links\nCensus\nEMPLOYMENT APPLICATION\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nCONTACT INFORMATION\nTelephone:\n660-885-7200\nPostal address:\n100 West Franklin Clinton, MO 64735\nE-Mail:\nGeneral Information: henry@sos.mo.gov\nWebmaster: Kelly Marriott henry@sos.mo.gov\nHours for the Henry County Courthouse\nOFFICES\nAssessor\nCounty Commission\nCounty Clerk\nCoroner\nRecorder of Deeds\nPublic Administrator\nTreasurer/Collector\nProsecuting Attorney\nEmergency Management\nAudit Report\nCircuit Court\nSurveyor\nLEPC\nJuvenile Division\nMonday - Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\nCOPYRIGHT © 2018 HENRY COUNTY, MO\nbottom of page",
